      "writtenOn": "2019-06-03T14:30:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Generally speaking, isConnected is almost never the right method to use, because it excludes things like SUSPENDED. I don\u0027t know if that can happen to VPNs though.\n\nDo we want something like vpnAgent.created here? AFAICS the UID ranges are added/removed only in updateUids(), which is called:\n\n- When the network disconnects\n- In handleRegisterNetworkAgent (just after the agent is created)\n- In updateCapabilities (presumably when the capabilities change, though IIRC this can\u0027t currently happen on VPNs without a disconnect)\n\nSo created seems like it might be more correct in the sense that it is updated whenever the rules are updated.\n\nHowever, generally speaking, callbacks only fire when the network goes into CONNECTED state. So if we want this code to match those callbacks, then vpnAgent.everConnected would be better than vpnAgent.created (and probably better than vpnAgent.networkInfo.isConnected()).",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1891,
        "startChar": 41,
