      "writtenOn": "2019-06-03T14:30:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "How is this whole loop (line 5911 to line 5948) different from simply doing something like:\n\n    for (final NetworkAgentInfo nai : mNetworkAgentInfos.values()) {\n        boolean metered \u003d nai.networkCapabilities.isMetered();\n        maybeNotifyNetworkBlocked(nai, metered, metered, mRestrictBackground, mRestrictBackground);\n    }\n\nIf it\u0027s the same, or if it\u0027s semantically equivalent, I would recommend replacing it with the simpler version I suggest, even if it performs a bit worse. VPNs don\u0027t connect/disconnect that often, and if this loop doesn\u0027t take too long, then I think it\u0027s better for it to be correct than for it to be as fast as possible.\n\nIf it\u0027s not the same, then... why? maybeNotifyNetworkBlocked looks like it\u0027s supposed to be idempotent and capable of calculating all blocked state for every request, because it calls isUidNetworkingWithVpnBlocked, which appears to take into account all state. So, if we call that method for every network on the system, presumably that should be enough.\n\nIf it\u0027s not enough, then why is it not enough? Is there a bug in maybeNotifyNetworkBlocked?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 5911,
        "startChar": 71,
        "endLine": 5911,
        "endChar": 72
      },
      "revId": "5eb643cec2b9258fdf5a4078644cf035ea4eff43",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
