    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1a8878ac_196b7248",
        "filename": "services/core/java/com/android/server/ConnectivityService.java",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 5911,
      "author": {
        "id": 1306837
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-06-04T04:48:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Consider a simpler example that we only have 2 conditions, data saver \u0026 VPN.\nSo we\u0027ll have two approaches to do this:\n1. use a single function that takes all information we needed. And pass current status to new/old parameter for unchanged parameters in the caller.\nmaybeNotify(oldDataSaver, newDataSaver, oldVpn, newVpn) {\n   oldBlocked \u003d oldDataSaver || oldVpn;\n   newBlocked \u003d newDataSaver || newVpn;\n   if(changed) notify();\n}\n2. or use a set of separate functions that only takes the information changed, and use current status globally stored.\nmaybeNotify1(oldDataSaver, newDataSaver) {\n   oldBlocked \u003d oldDataSaver || mCurVpn;\n   newBlocked \u003d newDataSaver || mCurVpn;\n   if(changed) notify();\n}\nmaybeNotify2(oldVpn, newVpn) {\n   oldBlocked \u003d mCurDataSaver || oldVpn;\n   newBlocked \u003d mCurDataSaver || newVpn;\n   if(changed) notify();\n}\nIf we are using maybeNotify1 for VPN changes event, the function cannot input VPN status change, but can only use mCurVpn. Thus the old/newBlocked might be both true or false based on mCurVpn. Thus, the callback cannot be fired since oldBlocked/newBlocked is always the same.\n\nTo reduce the parameters needed, we are using approach 2, where maybeNotifyNetworkBlocked takes the parameters other than VPN, and use current VPN status. By the example above we cannot call maybeNotifyNetworkBlocked. Is this making sense?",
      "parentUuid": "f0702b1a_a05ac5cb",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 5911,
        "startChar": 71,
        "endLine": 5911,
        "endChar": 72
      },
      "revId": "5eb643cec2b9258fdf5a4078644cf035ea4eff43",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
